# Copy to .env.local for `npm run dev`, and set the same two values as GitHub repo
# *variables* (Settings -> Secrets and variables -> Actions -> Variables) so
# .github/workflows/deploy.yml can bake them into the static export.
#
# PASTE THESE AS PLAIN TEXT. Both values travel in an HTTP header, so a single character
# that is not plain ASCII breaks every request with "String contains non ISO-8859-1 code
# point" - a message naming no variable and no file. Copying through anything that
# autocorrects (a doc, a chat client, a notes app) turns a hyphen into an en dash or adds
# a zero-width space, and neither is visible in the settings box afterwards.
# src/lib/supabase-client.ts checks for this at startup and says exactly what is wrong.
#
# Both are meant to ship in the client bundle: the anon key is not a secret, Row Level
# Security on every table (supabase/migrations/0001_accounts.sql) is what actually protects
# player data. Get these from your Supabase project: Project Settings -> API.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
